WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.900
The weaving cast-on is a quick
and easy way to start your knitting.

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:06.760
This cast-on is not appropriate

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:12.060
for garment edge, but it is a fast way
to start with waste yarn and ravel cord.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:12.880
When it's complete,

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:17.920
you'll see a single strand of yarn
running through the first row of stitches.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.900
Let's get started.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.660
Pull out the desired number of needles.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.040
With no yarn in the carriage,

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:28.340
run it across the bed to align
the needles in working position.

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:33.120
With your needle pusher,
pull every other needle all the way out.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:41.840
Engage both weaving brushes
and end up with the carriage on the right.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:47.540
Now you can thread your
carriage with your cast-on yarn.

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:49.760
Now grab the tail of yarn that's coming

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:54.500
from under the carriage and place it
across the top of all the needles.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:59.780
Hold the tail on the left-hand
side and knit across.

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:04.900
Hang a cast-on comb and a little weight.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:11.360
This will help form that first row
of stitches and continue knitting.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:20.850
You can disengage your
weaving brushes now.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.760
They're only used on that cast-on row.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:29.520
This is a very loose cast-on,
but it's perfect for swatching or any time

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:32.080
you want to get a very quick
start on your knitting.

